ependencies":[],"digest":"6bff60f1286073e31509a5fd4598d8079cf20026bee0ffe94d4a8e46c1dbc8e5"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T3","usage":{"input_tokens":285383,"output_tokens":4471,"requests":9}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name the concrete mechanism AC4 uses to capture peak RSS per gate run (e.g. cgroup v2 `memory.peak`, cgroup v1 `memory.max_usage_in_bytes`, or an explicit sampler), confirm it is available on the t4g.large host's cgroup version, and — if it is a capability gap — route the peak-RSS measurement to a short SPIKE before committing AC4/AC5.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.23,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC4: 'host and per-container memory, and peak RSS per gate run, are measured and queryable' — the mechanism (cgroup memory.peak/max_usage_in_bytes vs docker stats vs a sampler) is never named","repo search: GATE_PEAK_RSS, container_memory_rss_bytes, mem_available_percent, peak_rss, and cgroup all return (no matches) — this is a genuinely new measurement surface, not an already-used one","Contrast: AC1/AC2/AC3 map to already-shipped internals (observability.sh §1b mcp_healthy, monitoring_9ea3.tf alarm, autodeploy.sh mcp_retire_sweep guard) — those are not-applicable to T3","Peak RSS of a transient process cannot be recovered from a periodic 5-min probe sample (observability.sh cadence) alone; it needs a peak counter or per-run sampling that the plan does not describe"],"finding":"AC4 asserts a new capability — measuring and publishing PEAK RSS per gate run (GATE_PEAK_RSS marker) plus per-container RSS (container_memory_rss_bytes) and host mem_available_percent — without naming the mechanism that produces those numbers or verifying it is available on-box. Peak RSS is not directly exposed by docker or CloudWatch; it requires a cgroup peak counter (cgroup v2 memory.peak / cgroup v1 memory.max_usage_in_bytes) or an active sampler of a transient gate process, and which exists is host-cgroup-version-dependent. The plan leaves this load-bearing capability unstated, and AC5's entire OOM-sizing decision campaign rests on it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0304adc518b204d5","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — AC4 (and AC5, which consumes AC4's data)","norm_id":"nc43a8db1b4cedf9b","priority":0.67,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["cgroup v1 vs v2 on the t4g.large host exposes different (or no) peak-RSS counter, so GATE_PEAK_RSS silently never fires or reports current-not-peak RSS","the gate process is short-lived enough that a periodic sampler misses its peak, producing numbers that under-report the OOM headroom AC5 needs"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Either add an AC covering nginx failover/degraded-mode for a dead MCP upstream, or move root-cause item 2 explicitly into 'Deliberately NOT in this ticket' with a rationale tying it to the redeploy-recovery decision.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T5b","E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.5312,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"nginx's `upstream rebar_mcp` is a **single `server` line with no failover**, and still named the dead container's port, so every request 502'd\"","AC1: \"an unhealthy MCP upstream is detected and reported with an actionable signal\" — detection only","No AC adds failover / degraded-mode; the deferred list names only mem_limit, instance size, fan-out width"],"finding":"Root cause item 2 (nginx `upstream rebar_mcp` is a single `server` line with no failover) is identified as a confirmed root cause but no acceptance criterion remediates it, and it is not listed among the explicitly-deferred items. AC1 only DETECTS an unhealthy upstream; recovery still depends on manual redeploy. The plan should either add an AC for failover/degraded-mode handling or explicitly move it to the 'Deliberately NOT in this ticket' list with a rationale.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7035c715de5beeeb","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Root cause item 2; Acceptance Criteria; 'Deliberately NOT in this ticket'","norm_id":"n9aa191b1a3d02af1","priority":0.4188,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The MCP container crashes again; the alarm fires but nginx still 502s until a human redeploys, repeating the 12-hour outage minus the observation gap."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alte