rollout/rollback statement for the sweep behavior change appears in the plan."],"finding":"AC3 alters live behavior of the retire sweep (a deployed background process) so it no longer reaps a container whose port nginx still names, but the plan states no rollout/rollback story for this behavior change — only that 'redeploy is the only path back'. The retire-sweep change ships to 100% of the single deployed host with no flag/canary and no stated cheap revert.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f50257d72c4de2af6","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC3 / Root cause item 4","norm_id":"n3ba171580c31cf5c","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a one-line rollback note (revert to prior sweep logic via redeploy of the previous image/config) and note the change is idempotent/safe under the single-host deploy.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] For the retire-sweep / upstream recovery arm, state its failure-disposition contract: the c